{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l31gdkry","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 1 Offline","year":2010,"examDate":2010,"subject":"physics","chapter":"dual-nature-of-radiation","chapterGroup":"modern-physics","topic":"matter-waves-davisson-and-germer-experiment","type":"integer","marks":3,"negMarks":0,"permalink":"pan-alpha-particle-and-a-proton-are-accelerated-from-jee-advanced-physics-dual-nature-of-radiation-aviuvcelw6vyzgy3","content":"<p>An <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.448ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 640 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FC\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>-particle and a proton are accelerated from the rest by a potential difference of 100 V. After this, their de Broglie wavelengths are <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.027ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.319ex\" height=\"1.597ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 583 706\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D706\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D706\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container><sub><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.448ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 640 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FC\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></sub> and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.027ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.319ex\" height=\"1.597ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 583 706\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D706\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D706\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container><sub>p</sub>, respectively. The ratio <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -1.033ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.785ex\" height=\"3.372ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -1033.8 1230.9 1490.4\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(254.2,543.1) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D706\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D706\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(616,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D706\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D706\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(616,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D6FC\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FC\"></use></g></g></g></g><rect width=\"990.9\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, to the nearest integer, is _____________.</p>","options":[],"correct_options":[],"explanation":"<p>The de Broglie wavelength of a particle with momentum p is given by</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.027ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.319ex\" height=\"1.597ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -694 583 706\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D706\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D706\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> = h/p.</p>\n<p>The momentum and kinetic energy of a particle of mass m are related by</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"11.214ex\" height=\"2.619ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -963.5 4956.6 1157.5\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(780.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msqrt\" transform=\"translate(1836.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0,103.5)\"><use data-c=\"221A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-221A\"></use></g><g transform=\"translate(853,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45A\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1378,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43E\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"2267\" height=\"60\" x=\"853\" y=\"843.5\"></rect></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>.</p>\n<p>The kinetic energy of a charge q, accelerated through potential V, is given by K = qV. Thus,</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.652ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"27.487ex\" height=\"2.851ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -972 12149.1 1260\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D706\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D706\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(860.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1916.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"210E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-210E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2492.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"2F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msqrt\" transform=\"translate(2992.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(0,103.5)\"><use data-c=\"221A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-221A\"></use></g><g transform=\"translate(853,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45A\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1378,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43E\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"2267\" height=\"60\" x=\"853\" y=\"843.5\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(6390.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(7446.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"210E\" xlink:href=\"